<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;i&gt;I think the problem with &lt;c&gt;-bar&lt;/c&gt; is that it is difficult to disambiguate between the expression &lt;c&gt;'-' bareword&lt;/c&gt; and &lt;c&gt;'-bareword'&lt;/c&gt; as a single token.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hmmm... you mean like &lt;c&gt;-bareword&lt;/c&gt; and &lt;c&gt;-function_call&lt;/c&gt;? Since [doc://standard] requires parens on function calls, which is something I understand is probably going to be necessary for parseability, wouldn't that disambiguate the two? Or do you have another counterexample in mind?&lt;/p&gt;
</doctext>
